---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const capabilities = [
  ['Repository Intelligence', 'Build a structural view of Java and Kotlin repositories, files, symbols, and relationships.'],
  ['Dependency & Graph Intelligence', 'Trace dependencies, cycles, connected components, and PageRank knowledge hotspots.'],
  ['Git Evolution', 'Use authorship, churn, history, and evolution signals to add temporal context to repository analysis.'],
  ['Change & PR Intelligence', 'Connect source changes to affected areas, risk signals, PR context, and review follow-up.'],
  ['Architecture Intelligence', 'Inspect architecture signals, drift, and deterministic architecture contracts.'],
  ['Engineering Context & Reality', 'Create versioned context snapshots and deterministic identity across analysis and repository state.'],
  ['Grounded Repository Q&A', 'Retrieve bounded repository evidence before answering engineering questions.'],
  ['Prepare → Change → Verify', 'Create an evidence-backed plan and repository-bound Agent Change Contract, then verify against the persisted contract.'],
  ['Local REST & MCP', 'Expose the same local-first intelligence through Ktor REST and an MCP stdio interface for AI agents.'],
  ['Optional AI Assistance', 'Use bounded repository-derived context with a configured provider without making AI the source of repository truth.']
];
---

<BaseLayout title="Vericore — Evidence-grounded engineering intelligence" description="Vericore 0.7.0 provides deterministic engineering intelligence for Java and Kotlin repositories, grounded evidence, Engineering Reality, change safety, local APIs, MCP, and optional AI assistance.">
  <section class="hero container">
    <div class="eyebrow"><span class="pulse"></span> v0.7.0 · stable · open source · local-first</div>
    <h1>Understand.<br /><span>Change. Verify.</span></h1>
    <p class="hero-copy">Vericore analyzes Java and Kotlin repositories, dependency structure, Git history, architecture, and changes to produce reproducible engineering intelligence. It carries repository-derived evidence into Q&amp;A, planning, and a deterministic prepare → change → verify safety loop.</p>
    <div class="actions"><a class="button primary" href="https://github.com/sonii-shivansh/Vericore">View on GitHub ↗</a><a class="button secondary" href="#demo">Explore the proof</a><a class="button secondary" href="https://github.com/sonii-shivansh/Vericore/releases/tag/v0.7.0">Get v0.7.0 ↗</a></div>
    <div class="terminal" aria-label="Example Vericore analysis output"><div class="terminal-bar"><span></span><span></span><span></span><strong>vericore 0.7.0</strong></div><pre><code><span class="dim">$</span> vericore analyze ./payment-service

<span class="ok">✓</span> Repository indexed             <b>428 files</b>
<span class="ok">✓</span> Dependency relationships        <b>1,284</b>
<span class="ok">✓</span> Knowledge hotspots              <b>12</b>
<span class="warn">△</span> High-impact change surface      <b>3 components</b>

<span class="accent">Evidence</span>
  E17  PaymentService → PaymentRepository
  E21  PaymentController → PaymentService
  E34  recent change touches fraud flow

<span class="accent">Safety loop</span>
  prepare → Agent Change Contract → change → verify</code></pre></div>
  </section>

  <section id="capabilities" class="section container"><div class="section-heading"><span class="kicker">01 / CAPABILITIES</span><h2>From repository structure to a verified engineering change.</h2><p>These are capabilities implemented in Vericore 0.7.0, not future roadmap promises.</p></div><div class="capability-grid">{capabilities.map(([title, description], index) => (<article class="capability-card"><span class="index">{String(index + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</span><h3>{title}</h3><p>{description}</p></article>))}</div></section>

  <section id="architecture" class="section container"><div class="section-heading"><span class="kicker">02 / ARCHITECTURE</span><h2>Deterministic evidence first. Reasoning second.</h2><p>Vericore separates repository-derived facts from higher-level workflows. Analysis and Engineering Reality establish the evidence boundary; grounded workflows consume that boundary; optional AI reasons over bounded context.</p></div><div class="flow" aria-label="Vericore processing flow"><div>Repository + Git</div><i>→</i><div>Analysis Snapshot</div><i>→</i><div>Engineering Reality</div><i>→</i><div>Evidence</div><i>→</i><div>Q&amp;A / Planner / Verify</div></div><div class="architecture-grid"><article><span class="kicker">DETERMINISTIC</span><h3>Repository facts</h3><p>Structure, dependencies, cycles, PageRank hotspots, changes, architecture signals, PR intelligence, and Git evolution form the factual foundation.</p></article><article><span class="kicker">STATE BOUNDARY</span><h3>Engineering Reality</h3><p>Analysis is bound to repository state so stale intelligence can be rejected instead of silently mixed with newer source code.</p></article><article><span class="kicker">SAFETY</span><h3>Agent Change Contract</h3><p>The persisted prepare contract binds planned paths, evidence, verification, and repository identity. Verify checks that original contract after implementation.</p></article></div></section>

  <section id="demo" class="section container demo-section"><div class="section-heading"><span class="kicker">03 / PROOF</span><h2>Follow an engineering decision from evidence to verification.</h2><p>The production website uses committed sample artifacts so the experience is static, reproducible, and honest about GitHub Pages. It does not upload visitor repositories.</p></div><div class="evidence-card"><div class="evidence-header"><span>CHANGE PROOF</span><span class="status">GROUNDED</span></div><div class="evidence-body"><div><small>CHANGE</small><strong>PaymentService</strong></div><div><small>AFFECTED</small><strong>3 components · 6 test candidates</strong></div><div><small>CONTRACT</small><strong>Repository-bound SHA-256 fingerprint</strong></div><div><small>VERIFICATION</small><strong>Verify against the persisted prepare contract.</strong></div></div></div></section>

  <section class="section container launch"><div class="section-heading"><span class="kicker">LOCAL-FIRST</span><h2>Run it where your code already lives.</h2><p>Vericore analyzes repositories locally. AI is optional, generated reports are self-contained, and the REST server is intended for trusted local/internal use rather than public unauthenticated deployment.</p></div><div class="launch-grid"><article><span class="kicker">PLATFORMS</span><strong>Linux x64 · Windows x64 · macOS x64 · macOS ARM64</strong></article><article><span class="kicker">INTERFACES</span><strong>CLI · local REST API · MCP stdio · HTML reports</strong></article><article><span class="kicker">AI</span><strong>Optional, bounded repository-derived context</strong></article></div></section>

  <section class="cta container"><div><span class="kicker">OPEN SOURCE</span><h2>Explore Vericore 0.7.0.</h2><p>Read the implementation, inspect the evidence model, download the release, and contribute.</p></div><a class="button primary" href="https://github.com/sonii-shivansh/Vericore">Open repository ↗</a></section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
.hero{padding:112px 0 40px;position:relative}.hero::before{content:'';position:absolute;inset:0 -30vw auto;height:520px;z-index:-1;background:radial-gradient(circle at 50% 30%,rgb(115 213 255 / 10%),transparent 48%);pointer-events:none}.eyebrow,.kicker{color:var(--accent);font:600 .72rem/1.2 ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace;letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase}.eyebrow{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:9px;margin-bottom:26px}.pulse{width:7px;height:7px;border-radius:50%;background:var(--success);box-shadow:0 0 14px rgb(110 231 183 / 70%)}h1{max-width:900px;margin:0;font-size:clamp(3.2rem,8vw,6.8rem);line-height:.96;letter-spacing:-.065em}h1 span{color:var(--muted)}.hero-copy{max-width:800px;margin:30px 0;color:var(--muted);font-size:clamp(1rem,2vw,1.25rem)}.actions{display:flex;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap}.button{display:inline-flex;min-height:44px;align-items:center;justify-content:center;padding:0 18px;border-radius:8px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:650;font-size:.9rem;transition:transform .18s ease,border-color .18s ease}.button:hover{transform:translateY(-1px)}.primary{background:var(--text);color:var(--bg)}.secondary{border:1px solid var(--line);background:var(--panel)}.terminal{margin-top:72px;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:12px;background:#080c12;box-shadow:0 30px 80px rgb(0 0 0 / 30%);overflow:hidden}.terminal-bar{height:42px;display:flex;align-items:center;gap:7px;padding:0 14px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);color:var(--muted);font:.72rem ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace}.terminal-bar span{width:8px;height:8px;border-radius:50%;background:var(--line)}.terminal-bar strong{margin-left:8px;font-weight:500}pre{margin:0;padding:28px;overflow-x:auto;color:#cbd5e1;font:.82rem/1.8 ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace}.dim{color:var(--muted)}.ok{color:var(--success)}.warn{color:#fbbf24}.accent{color:var(--accent)}.section{padding-top:120px}.section-heading{max-width:820px;margin-bottom:42px}.section-heading h2,.cta h2{margin:10px 0;font-size:clamp(2rem,4vw,3.4rem);line-height:1.05;letter-spacing:-.04em}.section-heading p,.cta p{color:var(--muted);max-width:720px}.capability-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr);gap:10px}.capability-card,.architecture-grid article,.evidence-card,.launch-grid article{border:1px solid var(--line);background:var(--panel);border-radius:10px}.capability-card{min-height:190px;padding:22px}.index{color:var(--muted);font:.72rem ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace}h3{margin:28px 0 8px;font-size:1rem}.capability-card p,.architecture-grid p{margin:0;color:var(--muted);font-size:.88rem}.flow{display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;gap:10px;flex-wrap:wrap;padding:32px;border:1px solid var(--line);background:var(--panel);border-radius:10px;font:.76rem ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace}.flow div{padding:10px 14px;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:7px;background:var(--panel-2)}.flow i{color:var(--accent);font-style:normal}.architecture-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:10px;margin-top:10px}.architecture-grid article{padding:24px}.architecture-grid h3{margin-top:18px}.demo-section{padding-bottom:20px}.evidence-card{overflow:hidden}.evidence-header{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;padding:14px 18px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);font:600 .7rem ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace;letter-spacing:.1em}.status{color:var(--success)}.evidence-body{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,1fr);gap:1px;background:var(--line)}.evidence-body>div{padding:24px;background:var(--panel)}.evidence-body small{display:block;margin-bottom:8px;color:var(--muted);font:.68rem ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace}.evidence-body strong{font-size:.9rem;font-weight:550}.launch{padding-bottom:20px}.launch-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:10px}.launch-grid article{padding:22px}.launch-grid strong{display:block;margin-top:14px;font-size:.9rem;line-height:1.5}.cta{margin-top:120px;padding:38px;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;gap:30px;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:12px;background:linear-gradient(120deg,var(--panel),#0b1018)}
@media(max-width:1000px){h1{font-size:clamp(3rem,8vw,5.4rem)}.capability-grid{grid-template-columns:repeat(2,1fr)}.architecture-grid,.launch-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr}.architecture-grid article:last-child{grid-column:1/-1}.launch-grid article:last-child{grid-column:1/-1}}
@media(max-width:700px){.hero{padding-top:78px}.section{padding-top:88px}.capability-grid,.architecture-grid,.launch-grid,.evidence-body{grid-template-columns:1fr}.architecture-grid article:last-child,.launch-grid article:last-child{grid-column:auto}.flow{justify-content:flex-start;overflow-x:auto;flex-wrap:nowrap;scrollbar-width:thin;padding:20px}.flow i{flex:0 0 auto}.cta{margin-top:88px;flex-direction:column;align-items:flex-start;padding:26px}.terminal{margin-top:48px}.terminal-bar{padding-inline:12px}pre{padding:20px;font-size:.74rem}.hero-copy{margin-block:22px}.actions{width:100%}.actions .button{flex:1 1 180px}}
@media(max-width:430px){h1{font-size:clamp(2.55rem,14vw,3.5rem)}.container{width:calc(100% - 24px)}.section-heading h2,.cta h2{font-size:2rem}.capability-card,.architecture-grid article,.launch-grid article,.evidence-body>div{padding:20px}.button{width:100%}.evidence-header{padding-inline:14px}.hero{padding-top:64px}}
@media(prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){.button{transition:none}}
</style>
